Well, if you can easily kill a dragon in a standup fight, you should be able to
kill a shopkeeper, since whenever I have had a pet dragon they have killed and
eaten shopkeepers in a couple of moves.  From the stuff you listed (Stormy,
Excalibur, etc) if you have decent armor and such, I think you might be able to
kill a shopkeeper.  But why chance a good game on a gamble?  Surely you have
relieved a dwarf of his life and a pickaxe so far.  Want to have some fun?  Cut
a hole into the shop.  You will get a message that the wall seems to hard to dig
into.  Keep digging.  You will get through.  Walk in, pick up what you want, walk
out.  The Kops will come after you, but since you are invisible and a menace to
society, you should be able to knock them off with ease.  Make sure you fight them
in corridors as much as possible just in case.  If you run out of Kops, walk back
in and do it again.  Should be able to get a level or two without too much problem.
Oh, and try to fight your way to near a staircase, so you can run, just in case.
The shopkeeper will be pissed and demand payment, but unless you attack him, he
won't try to kill you.

